WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Organizers of the Route du Rhum, 2026 will spend 1.1 million euros securing the Saint-Malo Start Site alone, a 22-fold increase since 2014. This is Offshore North, Episode 7. Every four years, a small number of sailors set out alone to sail around the world without stopping or outside help, and one Canadian is working to join them. Over to the Canadian boat. As of the team's two September post, Emira 4 was now leaving Canada and heading back to Europe. Canada Ocean Racing,

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.540
releasing no new updates this week on the boat's position or preparations.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:38.700
The last known movement remains the transatlantic delivery to France after summer training on

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.220
the Great Lakes.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.380
Scott Shawyer's second September post detailed the summer's learnings on systems and handling,

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.480
but no further post have appeared in the 30-day window.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:51.600
The boat did not sail the defeat as a moot in Lorient earlier this month.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:57.380
With the route due rum start now 34 days away, the campaign's focus shifts to final preparations

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:57.940
in Europe.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:03.240
Scott Schaier spent the summer in Collingwood, Ontario, on George and Bay with Emir-a-4.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:08.560
A foiling, I'm Oka's 60 designed by Guillaume Verdea and built by CDK technologies.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:14.560
The boat arrived in Canada in spring 2026 after crossing the Atlantic and navigating the St. Lawrence

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.680
Seaway and Wellen Canal. Schaier described the biggest learning as understanding how the entire

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:25.700
boat works, from sails, rigging, and foils to electrical systems, hydro generators, solar panels,

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:29.540
signals, alternators, sensors, computers, and autopilot overlays.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.240
He learned these elements system by system and process by process in a controlled lake

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.380
environment he has known for over 40 years.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.600
On two heavy days his triceps sees on the grinder, which he trace to pushing rather than

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.860
pulling because of a shoulder injury and to not drinking enough water with electrolytes,

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.520
something he noted to monitor.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:52.720
He has not yet sailed in a mirror for in open ocean waves and swell and said he needs

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:53.520
to remain humble.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:59.320
The support team named in the post included Martin MSQA, who has been with the boat for a long time,

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.920
along with Gabby Bukow, Clovis Gutierre, Guyalina Bayot for rigging and systems,

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:08.720
Alberto Zacharia for electrical, computer and sensor systems,

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:13.660
Alan Roberts for coaching on the Exoset routing system, and autopilot overlays,

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.700
and Nick Maloney as sailing coach.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:20.300
The post also noted that the boat handles remarkably well in short period chop,

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.840
up, typical of the Great Lakes, with days of strong winds allowing quick sailing and

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.860
lighter days providing time for maneuvers.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:33.840
Emira Ford departed the weekend of 8-9 August, 2026 via the Welland Canal, earlier than

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.300
the published mid-August plan.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:40.820
The campaign's next major milestone is the Rout du Rums starting November 1st, 2026,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:46.120
from Saint Mallow, Shawier's first solo transatlantic race on a foiling IMOCA.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:52.320
Now, the fleet, the Rout du Rum 2026 presentation in Paris, revealed that securing the St.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:58.180
Molo site now costs 1.1 million euros compared to 50,000 in 2014.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:05.400
Organizers also face a 400,000-year-old budget for CSR measures, including a 100% electric

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:05.800
village.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:11.360
The business model relies on sponsorship rather than TV rights or ticketing, and the start

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:14.560
broadcast actually loses money at 500,000 euros.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:20.460
This escalation in costs shows how environmental and security requirements are reshaping the economics

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:21.940
of major offshore events.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:28.440
The 13th edition will feature 118 solo sailors across six classes on one start line from

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.120
Santa Mallow to Point Upitra.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:36.120
OC Sport Pendoux CEO Joseph Bizard noted that the event reaches millions of people every

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:43.440
four years, with Santa Mallow welcoming 1.2 million visitors in 2022 and Guadalupe seeing 300,000.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:49.140
The race does not rely on TV rights or ticketing, which normally account for 70% of such event

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:51.760
budgets, and instead depends on sponsorship.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:57.860
Producing the start and finish broadcasts costs 500,000 euros, creating a loss on TV.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:04.500
Site security in St. Mallow has risen sharply, while CSR investments now total around 400,000

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:04.820
euros.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:10.900
Covering Natura 2000 site demarcation, carbon assessments, educational work on environmental

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:14.600
financial issues and a fully electric village to reduce the carbon footprint.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:19.440
These figures come from an economic press briefing held the morning of the official presentation

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:23.060
on 22nd September at the Follies Bergeres in Paris.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:31.840
Jack Knife, the J-125, sailed by Sam and Andrew Hall, has entered the 2027 RORC transatlantic

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:36.940
race, building on their third place finish in the 2026 edition under IRC.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:43.760
The campaign moves from ISORA series success to a 3,000 nautical mile Atlantic crossing.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:48.620
Demonstrating how consistent preparation allows a Corinthian crew to compete against larger

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:49.120
yachts.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:55.220
The halls previously campaigned the Lombard 46 Pada Negra on the Irish Sea and retained

00:04:55.220 --> 00:05:00.700
the overall ISORA title, with Sam also receiving the Association's top youth award.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:09.100
Jackknife won IRC-2 and finished third overall under IRC in the 2026 RORC transatlantic race,

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:14.100
showing the boats effectiveness over a full ocean crossing despite lacking the latest generation

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:20.700
of offshore technology. The move from ISORA racing to the 3,000 nautical mile Atlantic crossing

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:26.360
represents another step in a campaign built on consistency, preparation, and crewwork rather

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:31.140
than outright speed. The boat has been a familiar competitor in Irish offshore racing,

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:36.100
including the ISORA series, where the halls develop their offshore program.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:43.640
In the 24-hour ultim, SVR Lazartig won the ultim class, while Eden Red took the Ocean 50 category.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:47.960
These short format races serve as final tune-ups before the route do rum,

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:53.780
testing boat speed and crewwork in a compressed window. The event took place on 26 September

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:58.340
and provided the last major gathering of the fleet ahead of the November transatlantic start.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:04.380
SVR Les Artigues victory in the Ultim Division and Eden Red's win in the Ocean 50 class

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:09.880
highlight the competitive depth in both the 32 meter flying trimorans and the 50 foot trimorans

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:15.220
that will share the Rout du Rum start line with the IAM OCA fleet. Time for plane sailing.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:21.640
The Rout du Rum starts all classes on one line from the 32 meter ultems down to the vintage monos.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:26.760
That single start line creates the festival atmosphere the race is known for, but it also

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.920
means the smaller boats must navigate the same weather systems and traffic as the giants

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.340
for the first 48 hours.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:38.040
The 118 entries this year will share the same departure from Saint Mallow with the fastest

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:42.560
boats pulling away quickly while the class 40 and vintage entries settle into their own

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:42.840
rhythms.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:47.600
This format rewards skippers who can manage their own race without being distracted by the

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:49.280
leaders disappearing over the horizon.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:57.000
The six official classes are Ultim, Ocean 50, IMOCA, Class 40, Vintage Multi, and Vintage

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:57.420
Mono.

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:02.360
Each class has its own target time, yet every boat crosses the same starting line at

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.040
the same moment.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:07.540
For a solo skipper, this means the first day and night are spent threading through a crowded

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:11.360
fleet while the weather routing decisions that will shape the rest of the crossing are

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.280
already being made.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:17.020
The format turns the departure into a single shared moment rather than staggered starts,

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:22.020
which is why the race draws such large crowds in St. Mallow and why the early hours often

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.580
decide who stays in contention, and the countdown.

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:30.460
776 days remain until the Vandeglobe start on November 12, 2028.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:36.320
The campaign's next milestone is the Rout du Rhum race village opening in 22 days on 20th

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:36.740
October.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:38.940
That's Offshore North for this week.

